                <pb facs="0676" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/2802: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Guaymas</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yepis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guaymas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-06T16:00:00-06:00">June 6, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of June 3, 5 p.m., I have been informed that the
                    definite dotation of lands in the Yaqui that were to be made yesterday were
                    postponed without giving reason for it.</p>
                <p>Embassy informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Yepis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
